        rules: {
          objective: "Form a 'Legal Hand' consisting of one identical pair and four additive pairs (totaling 10 or 20).",
          gameplay: '1. First player discards a tile.\n2. Next players can either take the discard (if it completes their winning hand) or draw from the wall.\n3. Every turn must end with a discard unless the player declares a win.',
          keyRules: [
            'Winning hand: one identical pair (eye) plus four pairs summing to 10 or 20 pips; the 4-2 tile counts as 3 pips.',
            'First player may discard without drawing; others may take a face-up tile from the table or draw from the wall, then discard one.',
            'Game begins with each player putting an equal ante into the pot; winner collects the pot.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Prioritize forming the 'Eye' (identical pair) early, as it's the hardest part of the hand to complete. Keep tiles that are versatile for 'Tens' (like 5s and 6s).",
          intermediate: "Watch for 'Dead Tiles': If three double-six tiles have already been discarded by others, your remaining double-six can never form an Eye and should be used in a total-sum pair instead.",
          advanced: "The 'Wait Rule': If you draw a tile that *could* complete a 10-sum, but it's a Military tile with no matching partner left in the deck, discard it immediately to avoid 'clogging' your hand.",
          tips: [
            'The four-two tile is the most flexible because its value change (from 6 to 3) allows for unexpected 10-sum completions.',
            'Always verify the number of sets in play; with 4 sets, the probability of finding an identical pair increases significantly.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
